4. useMemo
:Optimization hook , useMemo caches (memoizes) a calculated value.
: Normally, when a component re-renders, everything inside the component function runs again.

function App() {
  console.log("render");

  const result = expensiveCalculation();

  return <div>{result}</div>;
}

Render
↓
expensiveCalculation() runs again : Even if the calculation's inputs haven't changed.

For small calculations this is fine, but for expensive operations it can hurt performance.That's where useMemo helps.

const memoizedValue = useMemo(() => {
  return someCalculation();
}, [dependencies]);

If dependencies changed
    Recalculate
Else
    Return cached value


Importance :

Initial render
↓
Calculation runs once
↓
Value cached

count changes
↓
Component re-renders
↓
Calculation NOT run again
↓
Cached value returned


~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Cache Logic

const result = useMemo(() => {
  return num * 2;
}, [num]);

num = 5
↓
Calculate 10

num = 5 again
↓
Return cached 10

num = 6
↓
Calculate 12


5. useCallback
: memoizes a FUNCTION

useMemo  -> memoizes a VALUE
useCallback -> memoizes a FUNCTION


function Parent() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    console.log("clicked");
  }, []);

  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
        Increment
      </button>

      <Child onClick={handleClick} />
    </>
  );
}

Count changes
↓
Parent re-renders
↓
handleClick reference stays same
↓
Child sees same prop
↓
Child skips render

Dependency Array Works Like useMemo:
const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
  console.log(count);
}, [count]);

count = 1
↓
Function created

count = 1 again
↓
Reuse function

count = 2
↓
Create new function


Comparing All Hooks So Far
Hook	Stores	Re-render on Update?	Main Purpose
useState	State value	✅ Yes	UI state
useEffect	Nothing	❌	Side effects
useRef	Mutable value	❌	Persist data without render
useMemo	Computed value	❌	Cache expensive calculations
useCallback	Function	❌	Cache function references
